{"timestamp": 1779340514.4558342, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 29, "data": {"caller": "player_0", "reason": "Alice reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "lower_engine", "victim_name": "Eve"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779340514.4562483, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 29, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779340527.5021214, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 29, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I just found Eve dead in the lower engine. I've been running around doing tasks\u2014my route was oxygen, upper engine, medbay, electrical, storage, and finally lower engine where I stumbled on the body. \n\nSince Frank was ejected last meeting and the game hasn't ended, he must have been innocent. That means we have exactly one duck left, and it has to be either Bob or Diana. I saw Diana way back in security around tick 8, and Bob in electrical around tick 11. Neither of you have been near me recently. Where were you both leading up to this? Please explain your routes, because if we guess wrong here, the duck wins."}}
{"timestamp": 1779340548.7305527, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 29, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Alice, that sounds incredibly like a self-report. You just admitted your route took you exactly through all those left-side rooms and ended right where Eve died. \n\nAfter the last meeting, I started in medbay, went down to storage, but then I headed over to the right side of the ship\u2014through navigation, security, and then up to weapons and cafeteria. I haven't stepped foot in oxygen, upper engine, or lower engine this entire round. \n\nBob, we really need to hear your route. If you were nowhere near lower engine either, then Alice has to be the last Duck trying to pull a fast one on us by reporting her own kill. I'm leaning heavily towards Alice right now."}}
{"timestamp": 1779340580.5537434, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 29, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Diana, you just caught yourself in a massive lie. \n\nMy route this entire round was exactly Storage, then Navigation, up to Security, Weapons, and finally Cafeteria. I was doing tasks on that right side of the ship the entire time, and I didn't see a single soul\u2014including you. \n\nIf you had actually run that exact same path from Storage up to Cafeteria like you just claimed, there is no way we wouldn't have crossed paths or seen each other in one of those rooms. It's way too convenient that you tried to build an alibi on the complete opposite side of the ship from Lower Engine, but you just happened to guess the exact route I was already clearing.\n\nYou made up that right-side route to distance yourself from Eve's body. You had to have gone to Lower Engine, killed Eve, and then tried to blame Alice for a self-report. \n\nAlice, please vote Diana with me. This is for the game.\n\nDiana"}}
